    erkennung: `The sexual Five is the most intense, most passionate Five: withdrawn, but when she allows closeness, she goes all in. In my book <em>Enneagramm Zoo</em> I describe the image of the <strong>Hedgehog</strong>, immediately rolling into a ball at danger or emotional overload – protected in the safe tightness of its shell, and at the same time trapped there. Its spines are not an attack, but protection against the feeling of being overwhelmed.<br><br>Unlike the self-preservation or social Five, whose withdrawal is more practically or intellectually motivated, the SX5 seeks a deep, exclusive fusion – often allowed only in fantasy. Anyone who understands this reads her first reflex of withdrawal not as rejection, but as the attempt to protect a quiet longing for closeness from the fear of being overwhelmed by it.`,
