      text: `In our book <em>Führung mit Fundament</em> (which I wrote together with my son David L. Rathmer) we describe a Type Seven team leader who organizes a team event instead of addressing structural tension in the team. What helps here: grounding, commitment, staying with it. Leadership note: keep the Seven on topic – even when it gets uncomfortable.<br><br>Translated for the SX7, this means: the ability to lift mood and energy is a genuine strength – it only becomes helpful once it stops being an escape from necessary, uncomfortable conversations. Staying on topic, even when it's hard, often creates more real connection than any distraction.`,
