    notfall: "Suddenly stopping on one's own after prolonged use, particularly of sedatives or painkillers, can be medically dangerous and should take place under medical guidance. In the case of signs of overdose (severe clouding of consciousness, respiratory depression), call emergency services immediately. In the case of suicidal thoughts, contact a crisis hotline immediately. Addiction counseling services offer a low-threshold, confidential first point of contact, even when the substance was originally medically prescribed.",
