function bedeutungSubtypenPage() {
  return shell(`
    ${pageHeader("bedeutung-27-subtypen")}
    <div style="max-width:680px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 1rem 3rem;">
      <p class="eyebrow">Charts &middot; Subtypes & Typing</p>
      <h1 class="section-title">Why the 27 Subtypes Are Essential</h1>
      <p class="psycho-intro">Anyone who seriously engages with the Enneagram cannot bypass the 27 subtypes. It is a fundamental misconception to believe that one can initially &bdquo;just start with the nine types&ldquo; and add the subtypes later &ndash; because without them, the picture remains too crude for serious typing.</p>
      <img
        src="../assets/bedeutung-27-subtypen.jpg"
        alt="The Meaning of the 27 Subtypes in the Enneagram"
        style="width:100%;max-width:680px;display:block;margin:0 auto 2rem;border-radius:12px;cursor:zoom-in;"
      />

      <div class="vb-section">
        <p class="vb-intro">The nine types alone create caricatures too quickly. Type 8 becomes &bdquo;the strong one,&ldquo; Type 2 &bdquo;the helper,&ldquo; Type 5 &bdquo;the thinker,&ldquo; Type 4 &bdquo;the deep-feeling one.&ldquo; That may suffice for an initial overview &ndash; but it is not enough for serious type determination. Human beings do not live as stencils. They live as concrete, differentiated, often surprising expressions of a pattern.</p>

        <h2 style="font-family:'EB Garamond',serif;font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--ink);margin:1.6rem 0 .5rem;">The Nine Types Without Subtypes Lead Astray</h2>
        <p class="vb-intro">Those who work exclusively with the nine basic types run the risk of categorizing people too quickly. One recognizes certain behavioral traits, certain core themes &ndash; and thinks one has reached the goal. In reality, one often only holds a rough map. The actual landscape only reveals itself when the three instinctual drives are added: self-preservation, social, or sexual.</p>
        <p class="vb-intro">Only then does it become clear why two people of the same basic type can seem so different that on the surface, one would take them for two completely different types. A self-preservation Four can appear more objective and stoic than the common image of Type 4 would suggest. A social Eight can appear more caring and community-oriented than many expect from an Eight. A sexual Six can appear like an Eight. A self-preservation Two can easily be mistaken for a Six or Four.</p>

        <h2 style="font-family:'EB Garamond',serif;font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--ink);margin:1.6rem 0 .5rem;">The 27 Subtypes Are Not a Refinement for Specialists</h2>
        <p class="vb-intro">To put it plainly: In practice, we do not encounter nine types, but 27 manifestations of these nine types. The basic type remains central. But it never appears in the abstract. It always manifests within a specific instinctual dynamic, in a specific way of organizing oneself in the world. Anyone who considers only the basic type and ignores the subtypes is working with a skeleton &ndash; but not yet with a living human being.</p>
        <p class="vb-intro">Subtypes are therefore not a later remedy for advanced students, but a necessary part of understanding right from the start. They show how a type actually embodies itself, where its energy flows, and what colors its passion.</p>

        <h2 style="font-family:'EB Garamond',serif;font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--ink);margin:1.6rem 0 .5rem;">Typing Requires Agility</h2>
        <p class="vb-intro">A good understanding of the Enneagram does not thrive on stubbornly holding onto one level. It requires the ability to zoom back and forth between different levels. Sometimes you have to zoom far out: Is this person anchored more in the heart, head, or gut center? Then zoom in closer: Which of the three types within this triad could it be? And then look even closer: In which instinctual coloring does this type manifest?</p>
        <p class="vb-intro">This is not a luxury, but a genuine necessity. The number 3 remains important because of the triads. The number 9 remains important because of the basic types. But the number 27 is indispensable in concrete work with real human beings.</p>

        <blockquote class="pull-quote">The real question is not: Which type is this? But rather: In what concrete form does this person live out their type?</blockquote>

        <h2 style="font-family:'EB Garamond',serif;font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--ink);margin:1.6rem 0 .5rem;">Subtypes Protect Against Simplification</h2>
        <p class="vb-intro">Many people experience studying the Enneagram for a long time, reading a lot, knowing many type descriptions &ndash; and yet making no progress in determining their own type. They remain uncertain, waver between types, or feel that no description really fits. Often, this is simply because the work was too coarse.</p>
        <p class="vb-intro">Subtypes do not make the Enneagram unnecessarily complicated. They are what makes it truly realistic in the first place. They protect against the temptation to label people prematurely. They protect against type caricatures and superficial attributions. And they bring the Enneagram out of abstraction back into life &ndash; because a person is not simply &bdquo;a Four&ldquo; or &bdquo;a Six.&ldquo; They always live their type in a specific way. And this way is highly significant psychologically, energetically, and diagnostically.</p>

        <p class="vb-intro">Considering subtypes from the very beginning does not mean getting bogged down. It is about providing the right inner picture from the start: There are nine basic types, and each of these types appears in three fundamental instinctual variants. This knowledge alone changes one's entire mindset. Instead of learning nine rigid stencils, one learns a living, differentiated system right from the start.</p>

        <p class="vb-intro">Only in the 27 subtypes does a person reveal themselves in their true soulful form. Whoever stops at the nine basic types sees only the rough outline.</p>
      </div>

      ${bookTip("die-verborgene-dynamik-der-27-subtypen", "The 27 Subtypes in detail &ndash; normal type, intensifying type, and counter-type of each Enneagram type explained in depth.", "Die verborgene Dynamik der 27 Subtypen")}
      ${bookTip("wer-du-wirklich-bist-band-1", "The ultimate chart book: the nine types in colorful, illustrative overviews &ndash; the direct entry into the visual Enneagram.", "Wer du wirklich bist &ndash; Band 1")}
      ${relatedLinks([
        {route:"antriebskraefte", label:"Driving Forces of Humanity"},
        {route:"subtypen-schaubilder", label:"Subtype Charts (All 27)"},
        {route:"horney-triaden", label:"Horneyvian Triads & Subtypes"},
      ])}
    </div>
  `);
}


function bellaThornePage() {
  return shell(`
    <div class="page-container">
      ${pageHeader("Berühmte Persönlichkeiten")}
      <div id="js-back-target" data-route="beruehmte-persoenlichkeiten" style="display:none;"></div>
      <div class="krim-portrait-wrap">
        <div class="krim-portrait-frame">
          <img src="../assets/portraits/beruehmte-bella-thorne-portrait.jpg" alt="Bella Thorne – Portrait" class="krim-portrait-img" loading="lazy" />
        </div>
        <p class="krim-portrait-name">Bella Thorne</p>
        <p class="krim-portrait-typ">SO3w4 &middot; Social Type 3 with a Four Wing</p>
        <p class="krim-portrait-subtitle">Actress &amp; Director, born 1997 &ndash; Animal equivalent: Cheetah</p>
      </div>
      <div class="page-content">

        <h2 class="vb-section">1. The Cheetah</h2>
        <blockquote class="vb-blockquote">
          <p class="vb-intro">The <strong>cheetah</strong> is the animal of the Social Three &ndash; the fastest land animal on Earth. What distinguishes the cheetah is not size or raw power, but the ability to accelerate to full speed in the shortest possible time. No hesitation, no detours, just a direct leap toward the goal. The cheetah is an animal of the public space &ndash; it does not hunt in secret; it hunts on the savannah, visible to everyone.</p>
          <p class="vb-intro">The American actress Bella Thorne became known at age thirteen as a child actress with Disney &ndash; and has not paused since. Actress, singer, director, author, entrepreneur, social media star with tens of millions of followers. The pace is cheetah pace: always in motion, always present, always on the next leap. Standing still is not an option for the Social Three &ndash; it needs the run to feel alive.</p>
        </blockquote>

        <h2 class="vb-section">2. The Social Three: Visibility as a Life Theme</h2>
        <blockquote class="vb-blockquote">
          <p class="vb-intro">The <strong>Social Three (SO3)</strong> directs its energy toward the field of public recognition: status, reputation, and how it is perceived by others. Claudio Naranjo called this subtype the amplification type &ndash; the one where the Three themes of vanity and drive for achievement are most pronounced. The SO3 does not need a quiet territory. It needs the stage.</p>
          <p class="vb-intro">In Bella Thorne, this manifests with a consistency that impresses and sometimes overwhelms: she is everywhere. Not passively present, but actively shaping. She brought her OnlyFans account to over one million dollars in revenue within the first 24 hours &ndash; not despite public attention, but because of it. She has understood the rules of the game and uses them. The SO3 instinctively knows: visibility is capital. Whoever is seen exists.</p>
          <p class="vb-intro">Characteristic of the SO3 is also the courage to provoke as a strategy. Bella Thorne has repeatedly pushed boundaries &ndash; in her portrayal of sexuality, in her public disputes with Hollywood, in her willingness to speak the uncomfortable truth. This is not recklessness. This is the SO3 that has learned: whoever fails to stand out is forgotten. And being forgotten is the deepest terror of the Social Three.</p>
        </blockquote>

        <h2 class="vb-section">3. The Four Wing: Depth Beneath the Surface</h2>
        <blockquote class="vb-blockquote">
          <p class="vb-intro">The <strong>Four Wing (w4)</strong> brings something unexpected to the Social Three: an awareness of pain, of the incomplete, and of one's own inner world beyond success. An SO3 with a weaker Four Wing might appear polished &ndash; always glamorous, always optimized, always presenting the right image. The Four Wing breaks that open: here is someone who also knows the darkness &ndash; and is willing to show it.</p>
          <p class="vb-intro">In Bella Thorne, the Four Wing is visible in her unusual openness. She has spoken publicly about her childhood &ndash; about the early loss of her father, about sexual abuse, about dyslexia, and the challenges of her school years. This openness is not mere calculation &ndash; it is the sign of a personality that understands herself not just as an achievement machine, but as a human being with a history. The Four Wing does not just want to shine. It wants to be real.</p>
          <p class="vb-intro">The Four Wing also explains Thorne's artistic choices: she has taken on roles and directed projects that go far beyond what would benefit her brand. The SO3w4 seeks not just safe success &ndash; it seeks expression. This makes her more complex and contradictory than many of her peers in show business.</p>
        </blockquote>

        <h2 class="vb-section">4. Light and Shadow of the Social Three</h2>
        <blockquote class="vb-blockquote">
          <p class="vb-intro">The light of the SO3 is her energy and creative power. Bella Thorne has asserted herself in a profession that quickly consumes people &ndash; and she has never completely lost control of her own story. Starting at thirteen and already directing by her late twenties means she has accomplished more than most people twice her age. This is cheetah energy in its most creative form.</p>
          <p class="vb-intro">The destiny pattern of the Three is <strong>vanity / deception</strong> &ndash; the deep need to be perceived as successful and valuable, even when the inner reality sounds different. For the SO3, this manifests as the temptation to put the image above the truth: the perfect staging, the strategically placed minor scandal, the emotion performed for the audience. The boundary between genuine expression and calculated impact is one of life's most difficult questions for the SO3w4.</p>
          <p class="vb-intro">The Four Wing intensifies this field of tension: it brings the longing for authenticity &ndash; alongside the risk of staging pain as well. Whoever has learned that vulnerability generates attention must ask themselves: When am I showing myself, and when am I showing a version of myself?</p>
        </blockquote>

        <h2 class="vb-section">5. The Path of Healing: From Image to Person</h2>
        <blockquote class="vb-blockquote">
          <p class="vb-intro">The path of healing for the Three leads from the question <em>How am I seen?</em> to the realization <em>I am &ndash; even without an audience.</em> For the SO3w4, this means a dual step: letting go of the idea that public success defines one's worth &ndash; while simultaneously embracing the inner depth of the Four Wing not just as a source of interesting content, but as a genuine living space.</p>
          <p class="vb-intro">Bella Thorne is young &ndash; and her path of healing still lies ahead of her. But the steps she has already taken: openness about trauma, moving behind the camera, attempting to tell her own story rather than letting others tell it &ndash; these are signs that the cheetah already knows: there is life beyond the sprint. And that life could be the deepest she has ever lived.</p>
        </blockquote>

      </div>
      ${relatedLinks([
        {route:"beruehmte-persoenlichkeiten", label:"All Famous Personalities"},
        {route:"subtype/so3", label:"SO3 &ndash; The Cheetah: Subtype Profile"},
        {route:"beruehmte-cristiano-ronaldo", label:"Portrait: Cristiano Ronaldo (SO3w2)"},
      ])}
    </div>
  `);
}



